{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineId addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is a fenced citation on an explicit function with a body, and the commentary gives a substantive reason. The reason agrees with the current source.\n\n- **Where `node_path` is called.** It is called in only three kinds of production code. `graph.rs#fn[edge_fingerprint]` calls it, and `procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext]/fn[prepare_edges]` and `graph.rs#fn[dependencies_are_current]` reach it through that function. `agent/tools.rs` (`GraphSession` `node` and `dispatch`, and `ToolAgent` `run`) also calls it. All of these deal with graph edges or graph tools.\n- **The fixture has no edges.** The test `Project` domain's `outgoing_edges` always returns an empty vector, so no `OutgoingEdges` dependency is created and `edge_fingerprint` never reaches `node_path`. The `ProjectSources` session and the tests in this file never use the graph tools.\n- **Dependencies are node-only.** `mod[tests]/fn[source_capable_validator_tracks_deterministic_reads_and_reuses_saved_results]` expects only `Dependency::Node(\"source-node\", fingerprint)`. This matches the claim that mapped NodeIds are retained directly in dependencies.\n- **Other fixtures cover `node_path`.** The claim that stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains holds. `tests/contracts.rs` (`Relationships` and `Application`) and `tests/storage.rs` (`StoredGraph`, whose `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` call `node_path`) use their own domains. The graph validation tests and the agent tests use further separate domains.\n- **Why the method exists.** `node_path` is a required `Domain` trait method, which is why the fixture must define it. An unexecuted fixture method is a reasonable coverage exception.",
